{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_recurrence"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_dvd_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_dvd_iff","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse.lean#L219-L227","doc":"**Strong-divisibility equivalence (polynomial Fibonacci\ndivisibility).** For `a ≥ 1`, `b_a ∣ b_n ⟺ a ∣ n`.\n\nForward: `morganVoyceB_dvd_of_dvd`; reverse:\n`morganVoyceB_dvd_reverse`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_dvd_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_dvd_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse.lean#L176-L217","doc":"**Reverse strong divisibility of the Morgan–Voyce continuant.**\nFor `a ≥ 1`, `b_a ∣ b_n → a ∣ n`.\n\nMod-reduction: with `r = n % a`, if `r ≥ 1` then the addition law +\ncoprime cancellation give `b_a ∣ b_r`, contradicting the strict\ndegree bound `natDegree b_r = r − 1 < a − 1 = natDegree b_a`.  Hence\n`r = 0`, i.e. `a ∣ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_monic_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_monic_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse.lean#L144-L172","doc":"`b_{n+1}` is **monic** with `natDegree = n`.  Joint two-step\ninduction; the sum `X·b_{n+1} + b_n` has its leading term supplied\nby the strictly-higher-degree first summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_coprime_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_coprime_succ","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse.lean#L117-L140","doc":"**Consecutive continuants are coprime**: `IsCoprime b_n b_{n+1}`.\n\nInduction on `n`.  Base `IsCoprime b_0 b_1 = IsCoprime 0 1`; step\n`b_{n+2} = X·b_{n+1} + b_n`, so coprimality with `b_{n+1}` is\ninherited from `IsCoprime b_{n+1} b_n` by adding a multiple of\n`b_{n+1}` (`IsCoprime.add_mul_right_right`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_dvd_of_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_dvd_of_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse.lean#L108-L113","doc":"**Forward strong divisibility**: `a ∣ n → b_a ∣ b_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_dvd_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_dvd_mul","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse.lean#L93-L106","doc":"`b_n ∣ b_{n·k}`: the continuant of every multiple winding is\ndivisible by that of the base winding.  Induction on `k` from the\naddition law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_add","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_divisibility_reverse.lean#L64-L91","doc":"**Addition law** for the Morgan–Voyce continuant:\n`b_{m+n+1} = b_{m+1} b_{n+1} + b_m b_n`.\n\nThe polynomial Fibonacci addition identity, specialised to\n`b_1 = 1`, `b_2 = X`.  Two-step induction on `m` from\n`morganVoyceB_recurrence`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}